<item>
<title>Is Humor a Virtue?</title>
<link>https://www.spreaker.com/episode/is-humor-a-virtue--70000006</link>
<description><![CDATA[Aquinas thought a person who never jokes is guilty of a vice. Was he right? The Jesters work through <em>eutrapelia</em>, the old virtue of playfulness, and ask where wit ends and mockery begins. Michael defends the pun, Dan defends the Puritans, and Aaron tries to keep the levels even.<br /><br />Mentioned in this Episode: Thomas Aquinas, <em>Summa Theologiae</em> II-II, q. 168.<br /><br /><a href="https://www.instagram.com/jestersprivilege/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Follow us on Instagram.</a><br /><br /><a href="https://jestersprivilegepodcast.com/submit" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Send us a Question or a Confession.</a>]]></description>
