<item>
<title>Mockery and the Prophets</title>
<link>https://www.spreaker.com/episode/mockery-and-the-prophets--70000004</link>
<description><![CDATA[Elijah taunted the prophets of Baal. Isaiah laughed at a man who warms himself with half a log and bows down to the other half. When is mockery a prophetic act, and when is it just cruelty with a Bible verse attached?<br /><br />In this Episode:<ul><li>1 Kings 18 and the god who might be asleep</li><li>Isaiah 44 and the carpenter's idol</li><li>Why the Fool can say what the courtier can't</li></ul><a href="https://www.instagram.com/jestersprivilege/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Follow us on Instagram.</a>]]></description>
